      "math_academy_id": "q-103910",
      "knowledge_point_id": "dfbe689c-ae04-5405-9a38-d80f10662a0b",
      "knowledge_point": "Writing the Equation of a Horizontal Hyperbola in Standard Form",
      "problem": "Write the equation of the hyperbola $7{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=28$ in standard form.",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $28$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & =28 \\\\ \\frac{7{x}^{2}}{28}-\\frac{2{y}^{2}}{28} & =\\frac{28}{28} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{14} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
