      "problem": "Write the equation of the hyperbola $6{x}^{2}-11{y}^{2}=66$ in standard form.",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $66$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-11{y}^{2} & =66 \\\\ \\frac{6{x}^{2}}{66}-\\frac{11{y}^{2}}{66} & =\\frac{66}{66} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{11}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
